  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{ }x(y-1)\\,dy\\,dx=$",
  "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{ }x(y-1)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{ }(y-1)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}-y]}_{-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(\\frac{1}{2}(1-{x}^{2})-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}(1-{x}^{2})-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(-2\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-2x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}-2x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{2(1-{x}^{2})^{3/2}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =0-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
